---
/* One climatology document, folded once from the generated season and
   sliced client-side by the page script; filters never refetch. */
---

<section class="station-section" id="climatology" aria-labelledby="climatology-title">
  <h2 id="climatology-title">Climatology: the cube's views</h2>
  <p class="station-note">
    The same fourteen months folded once into a
    <code>StationClimatology</code> cube: every wedge of
    <code>&lt;meteo-climatology-rose&gt;</code> stacks by the document's own
    thresholds, the favorable share and coverage caption sit beneath, and
    <code>&lt;meteo-climatology-daily-pattern&gt;</code> re-sums the cube —
    the July filter refetches nothing.
  </p>
  <div class="station-filter-row">
    <div class="station-segmented" role="group" aria-label="Climatology filter">
      <button type="button" data-climatology-months="all" aria-pressed="true">Whole record</button>
      <button type="button" data-climatology-months="july" aria-pressed="false">July</button>
      <button type="button" data-climatology-months="winter" aria-pressed="false">Dec–Feb</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="station-grid station-grid-roses">
    <div class="station-panel">
      <h3><code>&lt;meteo-climatology-rose&gt;</code>: stacked wedges, judged ring</h3>
      <meteo-climatology-rose
        favorable-directions='[{"fromDeg":260,"toDeg":340}]'
        id="climatology-rose"
        station-name="Launch Ridge"></meteo-climatology-rose>
    </div>
    <div class="station-panel">
      <h3><code>&lt;meteo-climatology-daily-pattern&gt;</code>: the cube's typical day</h3>
      <meteo-climatology-daily-pattern
        id="climatology-pattern"
        station-name="Launch Ridge"></meteo-climatology-daily-pattern>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
